  "notes": "mg90-c, the second motor, through this notebook's cells as motor_model.py and brush_drop.py executed a second time by second_motor.py with every motor constant from mg90-c's own result files of rest-resistance, bemf-coast, speed-torque, no-load-current and inductance, each re-derived from mg90-c's captures; every key defined as in results/mg90-b.json's notes. No teardown number enters, since the coil runs, the delta and the brush photo are not run here. The locked motor is inductance's fast-1 at hole 11 (four fast groups, two slow) and capture-1 at hole 11 (slow), the bar seat rest-resistance's stall pass used, state C; mg90-c had no reversal run, so the slow decay is fast-1's slow groups and capture-1's, and motor_r_slow_ohm_by_capture carries capture-1 and fast-1 only. The motor_* ranges are the same union as mg90-b's, with the R variant that mg90-b took from the meter's ohms at rest taken from rest-resistance's r_stall_graded_lines_ohm (the ohms route was not run on mg90-c). The spinning points are bemf-coast's capture-1 rungs (state A, the ladder at 3.7, 5.0 and 7.4 V; the three cycles at 3.7 V 15 % that bemf-coast's mg90-c result leaves out are left out here too) and its meter-1 and high-1 points (state C, the DMM in series), with no spinning-1 points since mg90-c had no spinning run; g_spin_open_zero_ms takes capture-1's open zero per rung, meter-1's per point and high-1's 5 V level's, and its bounds are that value and the meter points alone. coast_over_meter carries capture-1's coast drag (state A) to the meter runs' ratio (state C). The grid's drag is capture-1's coast drag as a + b sqrt w, its rails 3.7, 5.0, 7.4 and 8.4 V as mg90-b's. drive_zero_counts_by_rail reads the dropout rows of capture-1, high-1 and speed-torque/capture-1 and has a 3.7 V row from three spins. The 100 % keys are speed-torque's capture-1, state A, and high-1's 100 % spins, state C. Left out against mg90-b's file: floor_edge_ma (the control's floor, a board read in the teardown sitting), bare_* and can_* (the coil runs) and delta_l_term_mh and delta_g_term_ms (the coil states), since mg90-c was not opened; running_r_incremental_ohm, since it runs speed-torque's estimator cells, which this section does not run on mg90-c",
